<!-- The M.D. Pa. Bankruptcy motion brief's Word styles: the cross-engine recipe (tools/fb/src/docxxengine.rs;
     docs/EVAL-LOOP.md, "Cross-engine gate") in the face of the typst template ({font}, Times New Roman; no M.D. Pa.
     font rule, see ../README.md) at 12 pt (size 24 half points); Body Text in exact 24 pt line boxes (480 twips, typst
     pitch-body: double spaced, as the filed brief) with a half-inch first-line indent (typst para-indent); single
     lines in 14 pt boxes (280 twips, typst pitch-single). docx/pamb.lua writes every paragraph itself: the court
     title, the caption (L.B.R. 9004-1), the title, the labelled headings, the signature block, the certificate of
     service (L.B.R. 9013-3) and the word-count certificate (L.B.R. 9013-2(b)), the footer (the page number, centred,
     its line box ending 0.5 in above the edge: typst footer-descent) and the section (letter, 1 in margins). Twips:
     20 x pt. pandoc-from: CommonMark with smart punctuation, as typst's cmarker reads the body. -->
<reference xmlns:w="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main" xmlns:r="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships" base="xengine" pandoc-from="commonmark+smart+pipe_tables+yaml_metadata_block" size="24" body="480" single="280" indent="720" heading="480" heading-before="0" heading-after="0" footer="720">
</reference>
